1
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:44,740
CONVERSATION 1
Hi, my name's Cathy, nice to meet you.

2
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:48,220
Nice to meet you too Kathy, my name's John.

3
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:50,120
I'm a university friend of the bride.

4
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:52,240
What about you?

5
00:00:52,240 --> 00:00:54,340
Who do you know at this party?

6
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:56,060
I am a colleague of Brenda.

7
00:00:56,060 --> 00:00:59,320
I was a little surprised to be invited to be honest.

8
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:05,060
We've only been working together the last six months, but we quickly became good friends.

9
00:01:05,060 --> 00:01:09,240
We just wrapped up a project with a difficult client last week.

10
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:14,320
I bet Brenda is glad it's done with, and she can focus on wedding preparations.

11
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:15,560
Oh, yes.

12
00:01:15,560 --> 00:01:18,320
So you are Cathy from the office.

13
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:24,760
Actually I've heard a lot about you in that project, the client sounded like a real nightmare.

14
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:34,260
Oh, he was, I mean we deal with all kinds of people on a regular basis, it's part of the job, but he was especially particular.

15
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:37,460
Enough about that, what line of work are you in?

16
00:01:37,460 --> 00:01:41,520
Well, right out of college I worked in advertising for a while.

17
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:46,680
Recently though, I turn my photography hobby into a small business.

18
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:50,940
I'll actually be taking photos during the big event as a wedding gift.

19
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:54,460
That sounds wonderful and very thoughtful of you.

20
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:56,740
I bake, just as a hobby.

21
00:01:56,740 --> 00:01:59,960
But Brenda has asked me to do the cake for the wedding.

22
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:04,640
I was a bit nervous saying yes because I'm far from a professional.

23
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:07,420
Did you bake the cookies here at the party tonight?

24
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:09,740
Yes, I got the idea from a magazine.

25
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:11,660
They're delicious!

26
00:02:11,660 --> 00:02:13,860
You've got nothing to worry about.

27
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:14,760
You are a natural.

28
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:16,460
You really think so?

29
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:21,100
If you hadn't told me that, I would have guessed they were baked by the restaurant.

30
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:27,360
You know, with your event planning experience you could very well open your own shop.

31
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:29,100
(laughing) One step at a time.

32
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:32,400
First, I'll see how baking the wedding cake goes.

33
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:43,980
If it's not a disaster, maybe I'll give it some more thought.

34
00:02:43,980 --> 00:03:02,600
Q1. What did Cathy and Brenda finish doing last week?

35
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:19,680
Q2. What is John going to do for Brenda?

36
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:37,540
